            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Urdu for to shrink, then the Urdu for to go stiff."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: پارہ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "پارہ — pārā — \"the temperature (in everyday talk); mercury\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "گرمیوں میں پارہ چالیس سے اوپر جاتا ہے۔ garmiyoṅ meṅ pārā chālīs se ūpar jātā hai. In summer the temperature goes above forty."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "پارہ (pārā) comes from Sanskrit pārada, \"quicksilver\" (Monier-Williams); the mercury in a thermometer gave Urdu its everyday word for the temperature."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
